<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aughnanure Castle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aughnanure Castle is a six-storey tower house near Oughterard, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a>, Ireland, built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oflaherty">O'Flaherty</a> lords of Iar Connacht in the 15th or 16th century. Standing on a rocky islet beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-corrib">Lough Corrib</a>, it is surrounded by a fortified bawn. It is now a national monument.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aughnanure-castle.jpg" alt="Aughnanure Castle" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christophe Meneboeuf · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aughnanure_Castle_(pixinn.net).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
